"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunkmhm_slotiva_docs=globalThis.webpackChunkmhm_slotiva_docs||[]).push([[674],{2690(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"slotiva-1-0-3","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-slotiva-docs/release-notes/slotiva-1-0-3","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-slotiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-11-16-slotiva-1-0-3.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-16-slotiva-1-0-3.md","title":"Slotiva 1.0.3","description":"Running the setup wizard again keeps your product\'s own settings, clearer limits, and help links to this site.","date":"2026-11-16T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"slotiva-1-0-3","title":"Slotiva 1.0.3","description":"Running the setup wizard again keeps your product\'s own settings, clearer limits, and help links to this site."},"unlisted":false},"content":"Slotiva 1.0.3 is a maintenance release. If you have already set up a bookable product, the most important change is that running\\nthe setup wizard again no longer touches that product\'s own settings.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## Fixed\\n\\n- **Running the setup wizard again keeps your product\'s settings.** An existing bookable product keeps its own appointment length,\\n  minimum hours per order and pricing. Step 3 tells you when the product keeps its own length, and the customer preview and the\\n  summary show that length. See [Setup wizard](/docs/getting-started/setup-wizard#step-3).\\n- **The summary always shows your service type**, also when you kept the suggested type without clicking a card.\\n- **One limit for the appointment length: 480 minutes (8 hours).** It applies everywhere you can set a length \u2014 the setup wizard,\\n  Slotiva \u2192 Working hours and the product\'s Slotiva tab. If a longer length was saved earlier, it does not stop you from saving\\n  your other working-hours settings. The wizard also refuses a price that is not a valid number.\\n- Activating Slotiva in a way that cannot open the setup wizard (for example from the command line or network-wide) no longer\\n  leaves an older \\"open the wizard\\" note behind that would send you to the wizard later.\\n\\n## Changed\\n\\n- **License screen:** the same views and texts as before, now with a help link under every state once a key is entered. The update hint names the\\n  current WordPress menu: **Plugins \u2192 Add Plugin \u2192 Upload Plugin**.\\n- **Slotiva \u2192 Settings \u2192 Bookable products** now says **Per slot** instead of \\"Per hour\\", the same as the product\'s Slotiva tab.\\n- **The payment check in the setup wizard** now says where to turn a payment method on: WooCommerce \u2192 Settings \u2192 Payments.\\n- Turkish admin texts now use the same informal voice everywhere.\\n\\n## Added\\n\\n- **Help links to this documentation:** **First-time setup guide** at the end of the setup wizard, **How to fix** on every\\n  checkout-check row that needs attention, and **About this license status** on the License screen. Admins who use WordPress in\\n  Turkish get the Turkish pages.\\n\\n## Updating\\n\\nDownload 1.0.3 from your account and install it via **Plugins \u2192 Add Plugin \u2192 Upload Plugin** \u2014 see\\n[Updating](/docs/getting-started/installation#updating). Your appointments, working hours and settings are kept."}]}}')}}]);